{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And the manna was like coriander seed.</b> The one who said this did not say that — Israel say, ״Our eyes are on nothing but the manna,״ but the Holy One, blessed be He, wrote in the Torah, ״And the manna was like coriander seed,״ etc. — meaning: see, inhabitants of the world, on what my children are complaining! And the manna is so and so precious:" "<b>Like coriander seed.</b> Round like a גִּידָּא — the seed of קוליינדר\"ו." "<b>Bdellium.</b> The name of a precious stone — קריסט\"ל."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {1 "קוליינדר\"ו is Old French coloendre, 'coriander'; גִּידָּא is Aramaic for a plant seed/berry.", 2 "קריסט\"ל is Old French cristal, 'crystal'."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:20.784136264Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}